const D57_C='D57 (required before any freeze is accepted; not met at R7A1-FREEZE-A1): a cap ends only after a week whose last executed exposure did its whole count after its time fit, and only when the cap is at or above the count the exercise would otherwise have next week, its normal count including any block-boundary set earned at that transition (phase reductions on top). No count after a re-establishment or a return exceeds the largest count executed since then by more than one set, at block boundaries too. At R7A1-FREEZE-A1 the return cap ends against the ending week’s normal count and after weeks fitted below their whole count (ssctr-r7a1-grid.mjs: 38 counts two sets above the largest executed since the return, 1 to 3; 8 return-cap ends after weeks whose every exposure was fitted below), so this clause is outside the approval until a later freeze meets it. Regression: the grid’s B, C and the ends-after-unwhole-weeks count at 0 over its 864 timelines, with the 20-minute RUNNING_SUPPORT returns.';
const D56_FINAL='D56 (final formulation, R7A1-SSCTR-r1 S1): a time-budget fit is not a phase reduction, but a week executed its whole count only when the last executed exposure of the exercise that week, the one that gives the week’s counts (R19, INV-04), executed its count before the phase reduction after its time fit. Any other week neither raises nor ends the regain cap (after a re-establishment) or the return cap (at and after the end of the return steps); the return ceiling (lastExecutedSets) is the largest whole count executed after the fit (R20). Met at R7A1-FREEZE-A1 for the rise of both caps and for the regain cap; not met for the end of the return cap (D57).';
const D58_C='D58 (required before any freeze is accepted; not met at R7A1-FREEZE-A1): in a short return the first quality slot after the break is the first quality slot still ahead of the return report, in the week re-entry starts or a later week; it runs easy, recorded as an adaptation of the week that holds it so a later re-plan and the weekly review keep it; exactly one slot is changed. At R7A1-FREEZE-A1 the rule reaches only the week re-entry starts: when that week’s quality slot is already past and two or more sessions remain, next week’s first quality slot keeps its quality dose (ssctr-r7a1-short.mjs: 96 of 315 cases, also after the weekly review; in a 10-day break THRESHOLD 41 where the last executed was 34), so this clause is outside the approval until a later freeze meets it. Regression: the short grid’s defects at 0 after the return and after the review.';
const R27_C='R27 / QE-R7A-02 (same-day reading, met at R7A1-FREEZE-A1): a session is still ahead of a review when it is dated after the review’s local date, or dated that day with no execution report while its chosen shift is not over; a morning (AM) session is over at noon local time, an afternoon or unspecified shift at the end of the day. A short return reported on the morning of a quality day, or the evening before, makes that run easy; an evening report never rewrites that morning’s session. The noon boundary is an operational convention of the shift model, not a physiological threshold.';
